# The toolchain the browser build needs, in the format asdf and mise both read.
#
# Until ADR-048 the build needed nothing but a JVM. It now also needs Node and pnpm, and this file
# is where their versions are stated (ADR-048 §6, R-1). `./mill frontend.solid.toolchain` reads it
# and fails with an actionable message rather than letting a wrong version produce a confusing
# build failure a long way from its cause.
#
# Node is a *minimum*: Vite 8 requires ^20.19 or >=22.12, and a newer Node is fine. pnpm is exact —
# `frontend/package.json` carries the same number in `packageManager`, and pnpm installs and runs
# that exact version itself, so the two must not disagree.
#
# Node was 22.12.0 here, and that combination does not work: pnpm 11.25 refuses to start on anything
# below 22.13 ("This version of pnpm requires at least Node.js v22.13"). Nobody hit it because every
# developer's machine happened to be on a newer Node than the file asks for — it only surfaced when
# a container was built to exactly these versions, which is the whole reason to pin them. The
# floor was then pnpm's, which is above Vite's, so one number satisfied both.
#
# It is now 22.19: jsdom's undici 8 declares `node >=22.19.0`, and from 8.10.2 it calls
# `zlib.createZstdDecompress` at load time, which 22.13 lacks — every vitest worker crashed on start
# and the test run reported 0% coverage instead of a failing test. 22.22.0 is the pinned patch.
nodejs 22.22.0
pnpm 11.25.0
